  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-16",
    "scope": "Two actually inspected western and south/tower exterior photographs,standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only.No bespoke research or redistributed reference images.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cattedrale_di_San_Giorgio_a_Ferrara.jpg",
        "author": "3impact",
        "date": "2009",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected full western front. Three nearly equal pale pink/cream marble gables,each with rose and stepped blind arcades; stacked narrow round and broader pointed galleries. Projecting central two-level protyrus has a large lower round arch,upper three-arch open balcony and sculpted triangular pediment. Three timber doors,slender dividing piers and two small open pinnacles. Fine saints/lion sculpture,inscriptions,reliefs and exact tracery are approximated,not copied into textures."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferrare_-_D%C3%B4me_-_Ext%C3%A9rieur.jpg",
        "author": "Jean-Christophe BENOIST",
        "date": "2024-07-24",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected whole long south side and most of campanile. Pink/cream striped square tower with four stacked Renaissance orders,triple round arcades,heavy cornices and no spire; very top partly cropped. Long lower brick wall has two arcaded bands above a low continuous tiled shop row. Three raised gabled volumes rise above side roofs;rounded eastern brick apse has pilasters and shallow dark cap. File description says Parme but title,coordinates and visible Ferrara tower/front support Ferrara identity. Temporary work fencing and adjacent town blocks are not modeled."
      }
    ]
  }
